    <unit id="reference.wire.lede">
      <segment>
        <source>An autonomous mandate is the open SD-JWT and the agent&apos;s closing token, joined by two tildes:</source>
      </segment>
    </unit>
    <unit id="reference.wire.root">
      <segment>
        <source>The open SD-JWT (typ dc+sd-jwt) is signed by the Trusted Surface. Its delegate_payload holds the mandate as one selectively disclosable element.</source>
      </segment>
    </unit>
    <unit id="reference.wire.closing">
      <segment>
        <source>The closing token (typ kb+sd-jwt) is signed with the key in cnf. It carries iat, aud, nonce and sd_hash, and discloses the closed mandate.</source>
      </segment>
    </unit>
    <unit id="reference.wire.hashes">
      <segment>
        <source>Every hash is the base64url SHA-256 of the exact characters sent. A receipt refers to the SHA-256 hash of the closing token.</source>
      </segment>
    </unit>
